+# A null holder raises `interpreter` when it is dereferenced, as the walker's
+# DEREF does (LMX_semantics.ru.md #exceptions): read by a condition (the raw
+# native route) and stored into a cell (the checked route); each block's
+# handler takes it.
@@ -18,2 +22,24 @@
-fn: observe_values (int: first; int: second; int: preserved) int
-    c.printf("V79 no-candidate first=%d second=%d preserved=%d\n", first, second, preserved)
